TabSheet2.Caption = Calculation
Label16.Caption = Smooth  normals:
Label18.Caption = DE stop:
Label22.Caption = Raystep multiplier:
Label13.Caption = Stepcount for \nbinary search:
SpeedButton10.Hint = Click on "M" to save these settings plus image width and scale\nas a preset. Click afterwards on "preview",  "mid" or "high"\nor again on "M" to cancel.
Label26.Caption = Stepwidth limiter:
Edit25.Hint = Defines the distance to the objects surface where raymarching stops.\nLower values gives more object details, but can also lead to undersampling.\nThe value is related to the width of a pixel.
CheckBox9.Caption = Vary DEstop on FOV:
CheckBox9.Hint = The distance to the objects surface, the raymarching stops, will get bigger with the distance to the viewer.\nThis leads to a homogen object appearence, so it is normally choosen.
CheckBox1.Caption = Normals on DE:
CheckBox1.Hint = Uncheck this, if the image looks flat and noisy.
Edit6.Hint = The distance estimates are downscaled by this factor to avoid overstepping.\nReduce the value if overstepping occurs (black pixels, noisy image).\nToo low values slows the rendering down.
CheckBox3.Caption = First step random:
CheckBox3.Hint = Multiplies the first stepwidth with a random number\nto give overstepping artifacts a noisy look.  \nAlso reduces banding in the dynamic fog.\s
CheckBox8.Caption = Shortdistance check DE:
CheckBox8.Hint = Useful for steep heightmaps
Edit8.Hint = Use values lower than 1 to reduce overstepping.
CheckBox2.Caption = Raystep sub DEstop:
CheckBox2.Hint = Subtract an amount of DEstop from next raystep, recommended on high DEstop values.
